It is Sunday afternoon and I am sitting on the sofa.
I am having my weekly video call with my family in Mexico.
I am holding the mobile phone in my hand.
My parents and my younger sister Sofia are on the screen.
We speak briefly about my week.
Then I show them my special guest.
Bruno is sleeping soundly next to me.
I turn the camera and show him.
"Oh, how cute!" Sofia calls out immediately.
"Please wake him up!" she says.
"I want to see him play."
I laugh and shake my head.
"No, Sofia," I answer.
"He is very tired."
"Let him sleep!" my mother says strictly.
"Mum is right," I explain.
"Small dogs must sleep a lot."
"We must not disturb him now."
Sofia sighs quietly.
"Oh well, then say hi to him from me later!" she says.
